
Starting MiniDos...

The disk in drive B is not formatted; FORMAT B: prepares it.
The disk in drive A is not formatted.
Format it now (Y/N)?N
FORMAT A: prepares it.
A:\>HELP FORMAT
Makes an empty file system on a disk

FORMAT drive: [/V:label] [/F:size] [/S]
  /V:label  The label of the disk, which FORMAT asks for unless given
  /F:size   The size of the disk in K, or in M with an M after it: 8K to 32M. A new disk
            gets 4M unless given, any other keeps its size
  /S        Puts the system programs onto the disk, as SYS does
A:\>COPY /?
Copies files, or joins them into one

COPY [/Y | /-Y] source [+ source ...] [destination]
  source       Files to copy, which wildcards may name; CON for the lines typed next, up to Ctrl-Z
  destination  A directory, a drive or a file name, the current directory unless given
  /Y           Replaces existing files without asking, as batch files always do
  /-Y          Asks before replacing a file
A:\>HELP NOPE
There is no such command; programs tell about themselves
A:\>DIR /Z
Invalid switch - /Z
A:\>CD /?
Shows or changes the current directory

CD [drive:][path]
  CD .. goes to the parent directory and CD \ to the root; CD drive: shows its current directory
A:\>CD..
The disk in drive A is not formatted
A:\>ECHO.

A:\>VER /?
Shows the MiniDos version

VER
A:\>EXIT
